    "text": "🌮Best Bites Berlin as someone who eats out A LOT 🍜  my current favs, save for later! week of eats Berlin💞\n\n #berlinguide #berlinfoodie #berlinrestaurant  ",
    "subtitles": "I eat out a lot, so here's everywhere I ate in Berlin this past week.\nMonday I had lunch at my favourite Korean in Berlin.\nIt's located on the iconic beautiful Oderbergerstraße in Pberg.\nThe bibimbap is to die for,\nthe portions are huge. They also have japchae noodles.\n10 out of ten. On Tuesday I went to check out a Chinese tea house and restaurant.\nThey serve Chinese tapas at lunchtime with a beautiful tea ceremony.\nIt's called Dot Tea Bar and located in Gleim Kiez.\nMake sure to try their cold noodles and main dishes at night.\nAnd they also have tea based desserts like matcha tiramisu.\nIt's so, so good and authentic.\nSave this for later as well.\nOn Wednesday\nI need a little pick me up from my favourite coffee shop in Berlin at bonanza.\nThey also have the best pastries.\nThe pain au chocolat taste like it's from Paris.\nThe pastries here are actually from 📍Canal Bakery,\nthe iconic bakery in Berlin.\nAnd the coffee here is just the best in my opinion.\nOn Thursday night I had a little date night with my boyfriend\nat my favourite spot in Prenzlauer Berg,\nthe Muschelbar. I think it's the only place like this that we have in Berlin\nand I'm so obsessed with it.\nI was feeling like on a little holiday we can trip to France.\nAnd it tastes like in France.\nSo I'll make sure to save this for later.\nAnd then on Friday, I went out with my girls and I finally tried munchies.\nI was there for the cheeseburger with cheese sauce and the biryani tacos.\nI tried the veggie version of the iconic hamburger and tacos,\nand I have to say, they are amazing.\nTaste like meat. Thanks so much for watching,\nand stay tuned for more vlogs like these. Bye!",
    "subtitlesLanguage": "eng-US",
